Concrete diagnosis: the scanner incorrectly excluded a number immediately
followed by an ASCII full stop, while including the same number before a
modern Chinese full stop. Raw "653. " lost token 653 but recovered
"653。 " kept it; the same affected all exercise-number prefixes.
Raw 663's final "0." also lost token 0, while recovered "0。" kept it.
All corresponding task quantities otherwise agreed.

Technical recovery: normalize only a dot not followed by a digit to the
modern full stop for numeric-token comparison, preserving decimal dots.
Math comparison remains exact and independent. Exact permitted-transform
comparison also remains independent. Only this scanner was corrected in
the next command; author/recovery bytes were never changed. This is not
an erased content failure, new author revision or second full review.

